# data/bench holds the run database and the precomputed corpus projections.
# Both are regenerated by running a benchmark - the projections take minutes and
# the database is per-machine state - so they stay out of git. The directory
# itself is kept via data/bench/.gitkeep.
data/bench/*
!data/bench/.gitkeep

# Compiled Python bytecode. These were tracked and rewrote themselves on every
# run, so they were a permanent source of noise in `git status` and a real risk
# of one machine's bytecode being committed over another's.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Benchmark logs written by the runner scripts.
*.log

# The Chroma vector store. It is a rebuildable index (~2 GB) regenerated by
# run_experiment.py, exactly like the projections above, so it does not belong
# in git and never did.
data/chroma_db/

# The HotpotQA training split (540 MB). It is a public dataset that can be
# re-downloaded, and it exceeds GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit.
data/datasets/hotpot_train.json

# Scratch output from earlier analysis passes, not part of the experiment.
# README.md documents these under "Untracked working files".
plots/
simulation/
run_token_count.py
visualize_results.py
tests/analysis_report.md
